You could try to a non-parametric method such as sign rank test but with
six arrays you do not have much power and the lowest nominal p-value in
this case is 0.03125.

Each statistical method has its advantages, disadvantages and
assumptions. Careful application of the correct statistics can be tricky
at times especially with small number of arrays where the assumptions
can be difficult to validate.

One of the problems I have working with biologists is explaining why
there is no one good method that works for all scenarios. The other is
of course the issue of design of arrays _before_ experimentation.

Given the dimension of microarrays, I am confident you can always
eye-ball problems like these with any statistic or method.



